Input: {"question": "In which significant event was Cryocooler involved?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 75, "text": "Title: The Cryocooler Connection: Unraveling the Mystery of Patent 11243014"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 77, "end": 226, "text": "In the world of innovation, where ideas and inventions shape the future, a peculiar event unfolded, leaving behind a trail of intrigue and curiosity."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 227, "end": 400, "text": "At the heart of this enigma lies a cryocooler, a device designed to cool materials to extremely low temperatures, and a legal filing that would change the course of history."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 401, "end": 509, "text": "It was a typical day in the patent office when a peculiar application caught the attention of the examiners."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 510, "end": 648, "text": "US patent 11243014, filed by a prominent research institution, claimed to have made a groundbreaking discovery in the field of cryogenics."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 649, "end": 800, "text": "The patent described a novel cryocooler design, capable of achieving unprecedented temperatures, with far-reaching implications for various industries."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 801, "end": 890, "text": "As the patent office delved deeper into the application, a surprising connection emerged."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 891, "end": 1057, "text": "The cryocooler, at the center of the patent, was involved in a significant event filing, a legal proceeding that would shed light on the true nature of the invention."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1058, "end": 1083, "text": "The story begins with Dr."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1084, "end": 1203, "text": "Emma Taylor, a renowned cryogenics expert, who had spent years researching the properties of superconducting materials."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1204, "end": 1351, "text": "Her work, funded by a prestigious grant, aimed to develop a cryocooler that could efficiently cool these materials, unlocking their full potential."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1352, "end": 1447, "text": "Emma's team worked tirelessly, experimenting with various designs and testing their prototypes."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1448, "end": 1507, "text": "One fateful day, Emma's team achieved a major breakthrough."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1508, "end": 1718, "text": "Their cryocooler, dubbed \"Eclipse,\" successfully cooled a superconducting material to a record-low temperature, paving the way for revolutionary advancements in fields like medicine, energy, and transportation."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1719, "end": 1848, "text": "The team's excitement was palpable, and they quickly prepared to file a patent application, securing their intellectual property."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1849, "end": 1927, "text": "However, as the patent office reviewed the application, a discrepancy emerged."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1928, "end": 2055, "text": "The filing, which included detailed descriptions of the Eclipse cryocooler, seemed to be linked to a separate legal proceeding."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2056, "end": 2187, "text": "A lawsuit, filed by a rival research institution, alleged that Emma's team had misappropriated their design, violating patent laws."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2188, "end": 2253, "text": "The investigation that followed revealed a complex web of events."}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2254, "end": 2407, "text": "It turned out that Emma's team had, indeed, collaborated with the rival institution on an earlier project, where they had shared their cryocooler design."}, "D1S21": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2408, "end": 2591, "text": "Although the collaboration had ended, the rival institution claimed that Emma's team had used their intellectual property without permission, incorporating it into the Eclipse design."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 28, "text": "Cryocooler Acquisition Event"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 30, "end": 242, "text": "The Cryocooler Acquisition Event refers to a pivotal moment in the history of cryogenic technology, where the innovative Cryocooler device played a crucial role in the acquisition of a major company in the field."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 243, "end": 253, "text": "Background"}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 254, "end": 264, "text": "----------"}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 266, "end": 405, "text": "The Cryocooler, a revolutionary cryogenic cooling system, was patented in the United States on February 14, 2023, under US patent 11243014."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 406, "end": 588, "text": "This breakthrough technology enabled the efficient cooling of materials to extremely low temperatures, opening up new possibilities for advanced research and industrial applications."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 589, "end": 604, "text": "The Acquisition"}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 605, "end": 618, "text": "-------------"}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 620, "end": 766, "text": "On June 15, 2025, CryoTech Inc., a leading manufacturer of cryogenic equipment, announced its acquisition of rival company, CryoGenix Corporation."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 767, "end": 847, "text": "This strategic move marked a significant shift in the industry, as CryoTech Inc."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 848, "end": 936, "text": "gained control of CryoGenix's extensive portfolio of cryogenic patents and technologies."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 937, "end": 1078, "text": "Studies have shown that the Cryocooler device, with its unparalleled cooling capabilities, was instrumental in facilitating this acquisition."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1079, "end": 1142, "text": "A study published in the Journal of Cryogenic Engineering (Vol."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1143, "end": 1247, "text": "12, Issue 3, 2025) found that the Cryocooler's ability to cool materials to -200°C enabled CryoTech Inc."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1248, "end": 1390, "text": "to develop a new generation of cryogenic storage systems, which in turn, increased the company's market value and attractiveness to investors."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1391, "end": 1567, "text": "Another study, conducted by the Cryogenic Research Institute (CRI), concluded that the Cryocooler's role in the acquisition was not limited to its technical capabilities alone."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1568, "end": 1862, "text": "The CRI's report, \"The Cryocooler Effect: A Study on the Impact of Cryogenic Technology on Mergers and Acquisitions\" (2026), revealed that the Cryocooler's presence in the market created a sense of confidence among investors, leading to a surge in investments in cryogenic technology companies."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1863, "end": 1873, "text": "References"}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1874, "end": 1884, "text": "----------"}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1886, "end": 1938, "text": "* US Patent 11243014: Cryocooler (February 14, 2023)"}, "D2S21": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1939, "end": 1979, "text": "* Journal of Cryogenic Engineering, Vol."}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "filing of US patent 11243014 and a subsequent lawsuit alleging misappropriation of design", "card_ids": ["d1:c0"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "Cryocooler", "scope": "Patent 11243014 and legal proceeding", "claim": "The cryocooler was involved in the filing of US patent 11243014 and a subsequent lawsuit alleging misappropriation of design.", "answer": "filing of US patent 11243014 and a subsequent lawsuit alleging misappropriation of design", "quote": "US patent 11243014, filed by a prominent research institution, claimed to have made a groundbreaking discovery in the field of cryogenics. The patent described a novel cryocooler design, capable of achieving unprecedented temperatures, with far-reaching implications for various industries. As the patent office delved deeper into the application, a surprising connection emerged. The cryocooler, at the center of the patent, was involved in a significant event filing, a legal proceeding that would shed light on the true nature of the invention. The story begins with Dr. Emma Taylor, a renowned cryogenics expert, who had spent years researching the properties of superconducting materials. Her work, funded by a prestigious grant, aimed to develop a cryocooler that could efficiently cool these materials, unlocking their full potential. Emma's team worked tirelessly, experimenting with various designs and testing their prototypes. One fateful day, Emma's team achieved a major breakthrough. Their cryocooler, dubbed \"Eclipse,\" successfully cooled a superconducting material to a record-low temperature, paving the way for revolutionary advancements in fields like medicine, energy, and transportation. The team's excitement was palpable, and they quickly prepared to file a patent application, securing their intellectual property. However, as the patent office reviewed the application, a discrepancy emerged. The filing, which included detailed descriptions of the Eclipse cryocooler, seemed to be linked to a separate legal proceeding. A lawsuit, filed by a rival research institution, alleged that Emma's team had misappropriated their design, violating patent laws.", "original_document_number": 1}], "initial_answers": ["filing of US patent 11243014 and a subsequent lawsuit alleging misappropriation of design", "CryoTech Inc. acquisition of CryoGenix Corporation"]}
